        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" ezremote:id="577" ezremote:identifier="intro" name="Summary" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><paragraph>Join the Exponential community: <link href="https://share.exponential.earth">forums</link>, <link href="https://doc.exponential.earth">documentation</link>, <link href="https://issues.exponential.earth">issues</link> and <link href="https://github.com/se7enxweb/exponential">code</link>.</paragraph></section>
        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" ezremote:id="578" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/"><paragraph>Exponential is built by its community. Whether you want to ask a question, help someone else, write documentation, translate the interface or send code, this page shows where to start.</paragraph><section><header>Ask and share</header><paragraph>The forums on <link href="https://share.exponential.earth">share.exponential.earth</link> are the place for questions about installing, configuring, designing and developing Exponential sites, and for sharing articles and tutorials.</paragraph></section><section><header>Report a problem</header><paragraph>Found a bug? Report it on the <link href="https://issues.exponential.earth">issue tracker</link>. Describe the steps that led to it, what you expected and what happened, and name the Exponential, PHP and database versions.</paragraph></section><section><header>Read and improve the documentation</header><paragraph>The guides, the help center and the technical reference are published at <link href="https://doc.exponential.earth">doc.exponential.earth</link>, in English and German. Corrections and new pages are welcome.</paragraph></section><section><header>Develop</header><paragraph>The kernel and the extensions are on <link href="https://github.com/se7enxweb/exponential">GitHub</link>. Fork a repository, make your change on a branch and open a pull request; continuous integration runs the tests on every supported PHP version and database.</paragraph><paragraph>Share your own extensions on <link href="https://projects.exponential.earth">projects.exponential.earth</link> so others can find them.</paragraph></section><section><header>Translate</header><paragraph>Exponential ships translations for many languages. Improve a translation or add a new one through the translation files in the repository, and send them as a pull request.</paragraph></section><section><header>Contact</header><paragraph>For hosting, support and development services, contact 7x at <link href="https://se7enx.com">se7enx.com</link>.</paragraph></section></section>
